"words that we can tie to a specific Hebrew or Greek word then get a dotted "
"underline."
msgstr ""

#: walkasjesus_app/templates/bible_study/bible_study.html:284
msgid ""
"Hover such a word and the matching original word lights up in the same "
"colour. Click it to open that word\\"
msgstr ""

#: walkasjesus_app/templates/bible_study/bible_study.html:285
msgid ""
"Words without an underline simply have no counterpart in the original "
"language, for example words a translator added to make the sentence run "
"smoothly."
msgstr ""

#: walkasjesus_app/templates/bible_study/bible_study.html:288
msgid "How the word links are made"
msgstr ""

#: walkasjesus_app/templates/bible_study/bible_study.html:289
msgid ""
"For the King James Version and the Dutch Statenvertaling the link is exact: "
"those editions were tagged word by word with Strong\\"
msgstr ""

#: walkasjesus_app/templates/bible_study/bible_study.html:290
msgid ""
"Modern revisions such as the Herziene Statenvertaling are matched against "
"that older tagged edition; where the wording still agrees, the link carries "
"over. Where it differs too much, no link is shown rather than a wrong one."
msgstr ""

#: walkasjesus_app/templates/bible_study/bible_study.html:291
msgid ""
"For other English translations there is no tagging, so the link is "
"estimated: every original word carries a short English rendering plus its "
"dictionary meanings, and the sentence is matched in reading order. This is a"
" best effort and can occasionally be off by a word."
msgstr ""

#: walkasjesus_app/templates/bible_study/bible_study.html:294
msgid "Where the data comes from"
msgstr ""

#: walkasjesus_app/templates/bible_study/bible_study.html:295
msgid ""
"Translation texts come from API.Bible and from the local Complete Jewish "
"Bible; every translation shows its own copyright line."
msgstr ""

#: walkasjesus_app/templates/bible_study/bible_study.html:296
msgid ""
"The Hebrew and Greek words, their grammar and their meanings come from the "
"STEPBible datasets (TAHOT, TAGNT and the brief Strong\\"
msgstr ""

#: walkasjesus_app/templates/bible_study/bible_study.html:297
msgid "The Strong\\"
msgstr ""

#: walkasjesus_app/templates/bible_study/bible_study.html:298
msgid ""
"When the site is set to Dutch, each original word also shows how the "
"Statenvertaling renders it here, plus a list of all its Statenvertaling "
"renderings with how often each one is used."
msgstr ""

#: walkasjesus_app/templates/bible_study/bible_study.html:299
msgid ""
"All of this word data is stored on this server, so studying words costs no "
"external requests and works even when the Bible API is unavailable."
msgstr ""

